1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,216
What if every bit of ice on Earth's land melted at once?

2
00:00:03,717 --> 00:00:07,753
Antarctica alone would raise the oceans about fifty-eight meters.

3
00:00:07,753 --> 00:00:11,541
Add Greenland and every glacier, and you get roughly seventy.

4
00:00:12,050 --> 00:00:14,687
London, Venice and the Netherlands go under.

5
00:00:14,687 --> 00:00:18,284
So does almost all of Florida, and nearly all of Bangladesh.

6
00:00:18,783 --> 00:00:21,086
Like and subscribe for more melted maps.

7
00:00:21,386 --> 00:00:24,747
Without its ice, West Antarctica wouldn't be land at all.

8
00:00:24,747 --> 00:00:26,928
It would be a chain of rocky islands.

9
00:00:27,417 --> 00:00:28,629
And the weirdest part?

10
00:00:28,629 --> 00:00:31,549
Right next to Greenland, the sea would actually drop,

11
00:00:31,549 --> 00:00:34,304
because the ice stops pulling the water toward it.

12
00:00:34,817 --> 00:00:36,575
So how long would it really take?

13
00:00:36,575 --> 00:00:37,960
Full story on the channel.
